# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tool output — CONTAINS CUSTOMER DATA. Never commit.
# Tools write hostnames, container images, pod names, namespaces and labels.
# These patterns are a backstop; prefer an --out-dir outside the repo entirely.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.csv
*.tsv
*.csv.checkpoint.json
*.checkpoint.json

# reports/ is the DEFAULT output location for every tool (reports/<tool>/), so it
# must stay ignored — that is where customer data lands.
# Other conventional --out-dir targets follow. All anchored to the repo root.
# Do NOT use unanchored globs like *-report/ here: that pattern also matches tool
# directories (e.g. tools/sdl-k8s-process-report/) and silently ignores the code.
# The *.csv rules above are the real backstop — they catch data anywhere.
/out/
/output/
/reports/
/report/
/k8s_report/
/s1_k8s_report/

# Anything explicitly marked local/scratch
/local/
/scratch/
/tmp/
*.local
*.local.*

# --- Credentials (belt and braces; tools read tokens from the environment) ---
.env
.env.*
*.token
*token.txt
secrets.*

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- macOS ---
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# --- Editors / IDEs ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- Claude Code ---
.claude/
